{
  "_doc": "Single source of truth for which games are enabled, surfaced to the web, and tested across the framework matrix. setup.py consumes sources verbatim; top-level CMakeLists.txt consumes id/enabled to add each game subdirectory, while each game's own CMakeLists.txt must keep its target source list in sync. tests/conftest.py / platform/game_service also consume this file. Schema per entry: id (str), enabled (bool, default true \u2014 disabled games skip build entirely), sources (list[str]; relative to games/<id>/, consumed by setup.py), capabilities (list[str]; tags consumed by the framework test matrix \u2014 see capability glossary below), framework_whitelist (bool, default false \u2014 true means the game must satisfy the core invariants the framework guards). To add a game: append an entry and add games/<id>/CMakeLists.txt. To temporarily disable: set enabled=false. Display order in the web UI follows declaration order here.",
  "_capabilities_doc": {
    "hidden_info": "Game has perspective-private slots (viz != all_public). Triggers tests that verify AI cannot read truth's hidden fields.",
    "snapshot": "Game registers public_state_applier \u2014 public state flows wire-side via PublicEventTrace.public_snapshot rather than via do_action_fast. Triggers public-snapshot round-trip tests.",
    "tracker": "Game registers a belief_tracker factory. Triggers tracker-consistency tests."
  },
